WEBVTT

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:15.420
Superman!

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.390
In the endless reaches of the universe, there once existed a planet known as Krypton,

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.730
a planet that burned like a green star in the distant heavens.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:12.330
There, civilization was far advanced and it brought forth a race of supermen,

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.960
whose mental and physical powers were developed to the absolute maximum.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.140
of human perfection.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.790
But there came a day when giant quakes threatened to destroy Krypton forever.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:24.000
One of the planet's leading scientists, sensing the approach of doom,

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.040
placed his infant son in a small rocket ship and sent it hurtling in the direction of the Earth

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.660
just as Krypton exploded.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.560
Rocket ship sped through star-studded space.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:40.250
Landing safely on Earth with its precious burden.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.030
Krypton's sole survivor.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.220
A passing motorist found the uninjured child.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.920
and took it to an orphanage.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.660
As the years went by and the child grew to maturity,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.360
he found himself possessed of amazing physical powers.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.080
Faster than a speeding bullet.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.760
More powerful than a locomotive.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.940
to leave tall buildings at a single bar.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.500
the infant of Fripton is now the man of steel, Superman.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.500
To best be in a position to use his amazing powers

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.480
in a never-ending battle for true justice,

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.320
Superman has assumed the skies of Clark Kent,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.230
mild-mannered reporter for a great metropolitan newspaper.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.890
Kent, I want to see you. Just received another.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.580
A threatening note.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:31.620
Okay, Mr. White.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.040
Lois.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:34.760
Another note from the Mad Antist.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.130
Coming in, Chief.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.120
Listen to this warning.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.000
He plans to strike tonight.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.050
Beware, you fools.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.000
My electrophanasia ray strikes tonight at 12.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:54.580
Total destruction will come to those who laughed at me and failed to heed my warning.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.010
Beware.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.710
I strike at midnight.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.620
This nut may prove dangerous.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.010
Kent, you help Lois follow up her lead.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.120
She may have an angle on this thing.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:05.950
Yes, sir.

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:09.720
But, Chief, I'd like the chance to crack the story on my own.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:12.920
Thanks, Chief.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.670
But, Lois...

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.130
Chief, don't you think that's a dangerous mission?

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:07.820
I'm a reporter for the...

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.050
The story.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:29.980
I'll give you the...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.880
the greatest story of destruction the world has ever known.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.860
How is that for a story to explain?

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:29.970
This looks like a job for s-

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.400
Superman.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.050
I don't believe it.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:38.390
Human!

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.380
Congratulations, Lois.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:14.860
That was a great scoop.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.980
Yes, Chief. Thanks to Superman.
